+  // Emit the trampoline pool now, if any forward branches are still
+  // outstanding. Call this immediately before opening a
+  // BlockTrampolinePoolScope that may span more than kMaxCondBranchReach.
+  //
+  // CheckTrampolinePool() returns without emitting for the entire duration of a
+  // blocked region, so a long scope does not delay the scheduled check -- it
+  // suppresses it permanently, and next_trampoline_check_ is simply passed.
+  // trampoline_ is then left at its default with free_slot_count_ == 0, and the
+  // first out-of-reach 16-bit fixup to bind afterwards takes bind_to()'s fatal
+  // CHECK_NE(trampoline_pos, kInvalidSlotPos). The scheduling leaves only
+  // kMaxBlockTrampolineSectionSize (64 instructions) of slack for blocked
+  // sections, but the baseline jump table and the Maglev/TurboFan deopt-exit
+  // loops hold one scope across the whole table: measured at 640,000 bytes for
+  // an 80,000-case switch, which is 80,000 * (b + nop).
+  void ForceTrampolinePoolEmission() {
+    if (trampoline_emitted_ || tracked_branch_count_ == 0) return;
+    if (is_trampoline_pool_blocked()) return;
+    next_trampoline_check_ = pc_offset();
+    CheckTrampolinePool();
+  }
